/E (Brain tumors are a major health problem worldwide, with characteristics of high morbidity and mortality. rates [1].The early and exact classification of the tumor type is of prime importance for the The optimal treatment strategy may range from surgery to radiation or chemotherapy [2]. MRI is a non-invasive imaging modality of choice which provides superior soft-tissue contrast. Clinicians usually diagnose tumors by mentally integrating information from multiple MRI sequences, such as T1-weighted\(T1\), T1-weighted contrast enhanced T1c, T2-weighted\(T2\), and Fluid-Attenuated Inversion Recovery \(FLAIR\), as each points out unique pathological characteristics [3]. Deep learning, especially 3D Convolutional Neural Networks, has achieved extraordinary success)
/Pg 7 0 R
/K [8 9]
>>
