/T (D. Ablation Study To empirically prove our hypothesis, we conducted an ablation study summarized in Table I, which verifies that both paths contribute to the final result. Both the specialized path with a result of 98.5% and the fused path with a result of 98.9% are strong predictors. However, their combination in the DPHF model yields 99.2%, thus outperforming both. This suggests that the features learned by each path are complementary and not highly redundant. The specialized path likely captures fine-grained textural or morphological details present in a single modality while the fused path learns the abstract "rules" dictating how those features appear across all four modalities.)
/E (D. Ablation Study To empirically prove our hypothesis, we conducted an ablation study summarized in Table I, which verifies that both paths contribute to the final result. Both the specialized path with a result of 98.5% and the fused path with a result of 98.9% are strong predictors. However, their combination in the DPHF model yields 99.2%, thus outperforming both. This suggests that the features learned by each path are complementary and not highly redundant. The specialized path likely captures fine-grained textural or morphological details present in a single modality while the fused path learns the abstract "rules" dictating how those features appear across all four modalities.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [16]
