/Type /StructElem
/S /H5
/T (It uses TensorBoard integration for visualizing in real-time metrics like loss, accuracy, and validation performance. Automatic checkpointing helps to save data in case of sudden interruptions. Moreover, the system will detect available GPUs and optimize computation on them to reduce manual work [2]. A lightweight Streamlit interface has also been implemented further for better interpretability and interaction with users: real-time visualization of classification results and Grad-CAMbased saliency maps. Such visual explanations enhance clinical trust and identify what specific MRI image regions triggered a particular decision of the model [3]The DPHF framework follows PEP-8 coding standards, supported by comprehensive inline documentation and detailed Jupyter notebook tutorials that reduce the learning curve for new users. Further, it supports multi-GPU distributed training and model export to TensorFlow Lite and ONNX format for real-world deployment. Structured logging, error handling, and pre-execution validation checks improve reliability, while version control using Git and DVC ensures full traceability of experiments.)
/E (It uses TensorBoard integration for visualizing in real-time metrics like loss, accuracy, and validation performance. Automatic checkpointing helps to save data in case of sudden interruptions. Moreover, the system will detect available GPUs and optimize computation on them to reduce manual work [2]. A lightweight Streamlit interface has also been implemented further for better interpretability and interaction with users: real-time visualization of classification results and Grad-CAMbased saliency maps. Such visual explanations enhance clinical trust and identify what specific MRI image regions triggered a particular decision of the model [3]The DPHF framework follows PEP-8 coding standards, supported by comprehensive inline documentation and detailed Jupyter notebook tutorials that reduce the learning curve for new users. Further, it supports multi-GPU distributed training and model export to TensorFlow Lite and ONNX format for real-world deployment. Structured logging, error handling, and pre-execution validation checks improve reliability, while version control using Git and DVC ensures full traceability of experiments.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [21]
>>
endobj
