317 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (The main purpose of the proposed DPHF framework should be to ensure that specifications are intact to maintain consis- tency, reproducibility, and reliability across different experi- mental settings. The architecture is designed to follow a modular structure that clearly separates data preprocessing, training, validation, and evaluation into independent, yet in- terconnected units. All model parameters, including learning rate, optimizer, and batch size, are clearly defined through configuration files; users can change the experimental settings without touching the source code. Docker containers, version control systems, and fixed random seeds maintain the con- sistency of environments for identical outcomes on different computational platforms. The implementation of the DPHF relies on Python standard libraries: TensorFlow, NumPy, and Pandas, following the guiding principles for software integrity stipulated by IEEE. The directory structure of the workflow is managed by the folders for data, logs, and checkpoints. Collaboration and experiment reproduction thus become much easier. Additionally, automated version tracking and model checkpointing ensure that no data or model state is lost in cases of interrupted training. By following strict configuration standards and open-source compatibility, the DPHF framework ensures that scientific transparency, consistency, and repro- ducibility in the long term are maintained.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
