/E (and affiliations section of the DPHF research paper follows the standard IEEE format, aiming to make it clear, uniform, and correctly indexed by digital databases. Full names of authors, including depart- ments, institutions, cities, countries, and email or ORCID IDs, should be clearly mentioned. Listed author names will be displayed from left to right and then top to bottom, showing the contribution order and ensuring consistency in citations across indexing platforms. Departments or divisions belonging to the same organization are not separated unless they rep- resent distinct entities, which keeps the text concise and professional in presentation. The affiliations are formatted in single spacing, listing the department name, institution, location, and contact information. The asterisk symbol * identifies the primary or corresponding author, including an e-mail address for technical queries or correspondence about publica- tion communication. Superscripts beside the author name denote multiple affiliations if needed. This structured and standardized format will help in cor- rect recognition of contributions, enhance visibility to institutions, and align with IEEE requirements on authorship and metadata. Clear author-affiliation structure will ensure transparency, accountability, and proper accreditation of persons re- sponsible for the development and validation of research work named as DPHF..)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [0]
>>
