/E (and tables stand as important representatives of the DPHF research paper, representing experimental re- sults, model architectures, and performance com- parisons in graphical or tabular forms. Figures and tables should follow the IEEE publication guidelines for consistency and readability. Figures include but are not limited to the DPHF architecture diagram, confusion matrices, and Grad-CAM visualizations; they are placed near their first citation and labeled sequentially as Fig. 1, Fig. 2, and so on. Every figure should have a descriptive caption, placed underneath, in 8-point Times New Roman font, describing what the figure depicts and why it is relevant. Tables present quantitative results, such as accuracy, preci- sion, recall, and F1-score comparisons with baseline models. They are numbered sequentially, with titles or captions placed above each table: Table I, Table II, etc. Large figures and tables may span across both columns. Axes should be labeled using words, not symbols, to avoid confusion. Use parentheses for measurement units where applicable. All figures and tables must be presented in high-resolution format to ensure that they are publishable both in print and digital. These formatting principles bring pro- fessionalism and clarity to the DPHF paper and are in accordance with IEEE publication standards.)
